{"agent_id":"pp3g-bjyI-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0541","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T20:17:23.868707895Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"af271565-c0d9-47bf-8888-339979ae59ee","comment_uuid":"60f29258-613a-4aab-ba14-0329c3a72e26","author":"pp3g-bjyI-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0541","content":"## Audit Verdict: NO DIVERGENCE OBSERVED\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n- [OK] — Document structure matches the task specification: original claims + 8 reviewer findings + Gemini synthesis, merged into a self-contained record. Section 2 reproduces the system description with corrections; Section 3 is the core claim-by-claim review (12 claims); Sections 4-7 provide consensus, invariants, WHAT-NOT-TESTED, and verified sources.\n- [OK] — Self-containment is achieved: the document quotes inline config values, plugin behavior, runtime evidence, and reviewer findings. A zero-context reader can reason over it without opening other files.\n- [OK] — Reasoning-certainty principle applied consistently: each resolution includes WHY (evidence basis) and WHAT-NOT-TESTED (explicit limits). The document marks unverified claims as (unverified) rather than asserting them.\n\n### Process Assessment\n- [OK] — Builder pp3g-4hUs produced a 1737-line document within the 30m timeout. The builder's tmux session was running (confirmed via crosslink agent prompt). The builder posted position comments on #320.\n- [OK] — No stale position: builder was actively producing output throughout the session.\n- [CONCERN] — Builder used deepseek-v4-flash (free model) which initially appeared non-responsive (no commits for ~7 minutes). The builder was actually working through a tmux session that wasn't visible via crosslink kickoff list. This is a monitoring gap: the pre-positioned auditor initially could not detect the builder's activity.\n\n### Spot-Check Results (13 source claims verified)\n1. Crosslink version: 0.9.0-beta.1+a87bd513 (deployed) vs v0.9.0-beta.1-59-g6221309e (source HEAD) — CORRECT\n2. Opencode version: 1.18.13-pp3g-fork — CORRECT\n3. Rtk version: 0.40.0 — CORRECT\n4. allowed_bash_prefixes: 49 entries — CORRECT (verified line-by-line)\n5. agent_overrides.blocked_git_commands: 21 entries — CORRECT\n6. Orchestrator bash allow patterns: 34 — CORRECT\n7. Root blocked_git_commands: 14 — CORRECT\n8. No by_type.builder entry in hook-config — CORRECT\n9. MCP tool names: filesystem_write_file/filesystem_edit_file are real (runtime-log-verified, 51+107 entries); create_directory/move_file unblocked — CORRECT\n10. Wrapper --auto injection: lines 66-68 inject under tmux — CORRECT\n11. Wrapper --allowedTools drop: lines 28-30 consume with shift 2 — CORRECT\n12. Identity fallback to builder: resolveAgentType returns 'builder' when absent — CORRECT\n13. Main repo agent.json role: 'driver' (agent_overrides skipped) — CORRECT\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n- Risk: Free-model builder launches may appear non-responsive to pre-positioned auditors (no kickoff agent registration, tmux session invisible to crosslink kickoff list) — Impact: monitoring gap; auditor may falsely flag staleness — Recommended mitigation: ensure builders launched as tmux sessions register with crosslink kickoff list, or auditors check tmux sessions directly\n- Risk: The document's 1737 lines may exceed comfortable review scope for some consumers — Impact: review fatigue; key findings may be missed — Recommended mitigation: consider a 1-page executive summary for operator consumption\n\n### Recommendations\n- Improvement: Add a one-page executive summary at the top for the operator — Rationale: 1737 lines is thorough but dense; operator needs the key takeaways quickly — Priority: medium\n- Improvement: The builder should register tmux sessions with crosslink kickoff list for auditor visibility — Rationale: the pre-positioned auditor pattern depends on detecting builder activity; tmux-only sessions are invisible — Priority: high (process improvement)\n\n### WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n- No live bypass demonstrations were performed (all findings are capability inferences from source reading)\n- The container path for --allowedTools was not tested (only the local tmux path)\n- Whether --auto actually converts ask permissions to allow (vs only auto-consenting) was not empirically confirmed\n- Hook ordering between plugins was not measured\n- The models-cache.json contents were not audited for re-enabled providers\n","created_at":"2026-08-09T20:17:23.861670887Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:uk5fieOV2PqG3+gwmxtWd6kJ1W+4dh2XiXRmTCe6ctE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJqVotiiW7Q2dg9vcnavtYtXW56qUuvvh2YC8VadGvs0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA9cKdJVEalQd4LTWSLJGxb3a3lsGPIzEZxWxKQlEOS5dbIYP3MErBeJNqUlzZvsvz0l0qz1JHL6TVT8L/irE0AQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:uk5fieOV2PqG3+gwmxtWd6kJ1W+4dh2XiXRmTCe6ctE","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgJqVotiiW7Q2dg9vcnavtYtXW56qUuvvh2YC8VadGvs0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQArPT4SS8z54u1ulQsH25uxSO6zYs4mHkaAXFFfechiYQJ5skeoyNITsKTO5HFjghTEb/QQ0bYWyA3XZqDy4hgk="}
